WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.998 --> 00:00:16.685
The window was open, so I knew Pap had climbed in using the shed.

2
00:00:17.505 --> 00:00:19.627
For a while we just looked at each other.

3
00:00:20.627 --> 00:00:24.370
I used to be scared of Pap all the time because he beat me so much.

4
00:00:25.251 --> 00:00:29.433
I was scared now, for a minute, but then I looked at him more closely.

5
00:00:30.774 --> 00:00:34.501
Pap was about fifty years old now, and he looked his age.

6
00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:40.606
His skin was as white as a fish belly, and he had long tangled greasy black hair.

7
00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:46.030
His clothes were just rags, and his toes stuck out through the ends of his boots.

8
00:00:47.832 --> 00:00:51.555
Finally Pap said, "Those are starchy clothes you're wearing.

9
00:00:52.215 --> 00:00:55.338
You're educated too, they say—you can read and write.

10
00:00:56.219 --> 00:00:59.401
You think you're better than your father now, don't you, because I can't read?

11
00:01:00.402 --> 00:01:02.704
Who told you that you could do this foolishness, huh?"

12
00:01:03.488 --> 00:01:04.328
"The Widow Douglas.

13
00:01:04.848 --> 00:01:06.429
She told me," I said.

14
00:01:06.449 --> 00:01:08.249
"The widow, huh?

15
00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:10.770
Well, I'll teach her not to interfere.

16
00:01:11.790 --> 00:01:12.390
And listen to me.

17
00:01:12.931 --> 00:01:15.351
You drop that school or I'll give you a beating.

18
00:01:16.031 --> 00:01:19.412
I won't let people bring up a boy to think he's better than his own father!

19
00:01:20.173 --> 00:01:21.593
Say, let me hear you read."

20
00:01:22.433 --> 00:01:24.874
I picked up a book and began to read aloud.

21
00:01:27.415 --> 00:01:30.155
After half a minute, he knocked the book out of my hand.

22
00:01:30.175 --> 00:01:32.596
"It's true," he said.

23
00:01:33.336 --> 00:01:34.017
"You can do it."

24
00:01:34.777 --> 00:01:40.460
Then he went on, "I see you have a bed, a mirror, and a carpet on the floor—while

25
00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:42.281
your own father has to sleep with the pigs.

26
00:01:43.022 --> 00:01:45.863
I've been in town for two days, and I keep hearing that you're rich.

27
00:01:46.564 --> 00:01:47.444
That's why I came."

28
00:01:47.464 --> 00:01:51.066
"I don't have any money," I said.

29
00:01:51.086 --> 00:01:53.047
"That's a lie.

30
00:01:53.507 --> 00:01:54.948
Judge Thatcher is keeping it for you.

31
00:01:55.609 --> 00:01:57.029
You get me that money tomorrow.

32
00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:57.650
I want it!"

33
00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:01.392
Then Pap made me give him the dollar I had in my pocket.

34
00:02:02.036 --> 00:02:04.557
He said he was going to town to get some whiskey.

35
00:02:06.458 --> 00:02:07.999
The next day Pap was drunk.

36
00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:13.362
He went to Judge Thatcher's and threatened him, but Judge Thatcher wouldn't give him the money.

37
00:02:14.823 --> 00:02:19.846
Judge Thatcher and the Widow Douglas wanted to take me away from Pap and have one of them

38
00:02:19.886 --> 00:02:20.606
be my guardian.

39
00:02:21.446 --> 00:02:24.828
There was a new judge in court, however, who had just come to town.

40
00:02:25.969 --> 00:02:27.870
He didn't know what my father was like.

41
00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:31.712
The judge said that the courts shouldn't split up families.

42
00:02:32.884 --> 00:02:34.605
He said that I had to stay with Pap.

43
00:02:36.525 --> 00:02:41.087
As soon as my father heard this, he told me that he'd beat me until I was covered

44
00:02:41.107 --> 00:02:43.347
with bruises unless I got him some money.

45
00:02:45.708 --> 00:02:50.310
I borrowed three dollars from Judge Thatcher and gave it to Pap, and he used the money to

46
00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:50.930
get drunk.

47
00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:56.892
Later at night he made so much noise in the street that he was arrested and put in

48
00:02:56.972 --> 00:02:57.932
jail for a week.

49
00:02:59.188 --> 00:03:02.771
When Pap got out of jail, the new judge still thought he could help him.

50
00:03:03.712 --> 00:03:07.395
He took Pap into his own home, fed him, and gave him new clothes.

51
00:03:09.457 --> 00:03:12.299
Pap cried and promised that he would become a better man.

52
00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:18.724
The judge and his family believed him, but after a couple of days, my father traded his new

53
00:03:18.805 --> 00:03:21.187
coat for whiskey and got drunk again.

54
00:03:22.608 --> 00:03:25.790
He fell off the judge's porch and broke his arm in two places.

55
00:03:26.971 --> 00:03:29.758
After that, the judge stopped trying to help Pap.

56
00:03:31.299 --> 00:03:34.962
I still lived at the Widow Douglas' house, and I still went to school.

57
00:03:36.083 --> 00:03:40.206
But when Pap's arm was healed, he started chasing me again and demanding money.

58
00:03:41.027 --> 00:03:42.528
If I didn't have any, he'd hit me.

59
00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:47.933
So I started to borrow money from Judge Thatcher and give it to Pap.

60
00:03:50.135 --> 00:03:53.978
Then he'd buy whiskey, get drunk, and be sent to jail for a few days.

61
00:03:54.999 --> 00:03:56.160
This went on for a while.

62
00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:02.462
Finally, one day in the spring, Pap grabbed me and took me up the river in a small

63
00:04:02.502 --> 00:04:09.205
boat. We landed at a place where there were no houses—just an old log hut hidden in the

64
00:04:09.245 --> 00:04:14.408
woods. Pap kept me with him all the time, and I never got a chance to run away.

65
00:04:15.408 --> 00:04:19.130
He always locked the door and he put the key under his head when he slept.

66
00:04:19.990 --> 00:04:23.032
We fished and hunted, and that was how we got food.

67
00:04:24.412 --> 00:04:28.596
Sometimes Pap locked me in the cabin and traveled down the river to a store.

68
00:04:29.476 --> 00:04:32.859
There he traded our fish and the animals we killed for whiskey.

69
00:04:34.401 --> 00:04:38.364
I began to enjoy my new lazy life with no books or studying.

70
00:04:39.225 --> 00:04:42.467
Two months went by and my clothes were all dirty rags again.

71
00:04:43.608 --> 00:04:49.133
I couldn't understand how I'd ever liked my life at the widow's house, where I had to wash,

72
00:04:49.513 --> 00:04:52.316
eat off a plate, and go to bed at a regular time.

73
00:04:53.892 --> 00:04:55.594
But Pap's behavior became worse.

74
00:04:56.455 --> 00:04:59.178
He beat me so much that I had bruises all over me.

75
00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:03.322
One time he went away and left me locked up for three days.

76
00:05:04.623 --> 00:05:07.306
I made up my mind that I would have to get away from him.

77
00:05:08.527 --> 00:05:08.968
But how?
